Z||000000||mutfish||11-20-1999||11:42 PM||||Just replaced the clutch master cylinder in my '88gt...going flush the system and use dot-5 silicone fluid,has anyone heard any pros or cons on this practice. I have used it in corvette brake system that is stored for long periods with good results.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||11-21-1999||01:00 AM||||<BR>You might want to hold off on using the Dot-5 until you read this thread:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034.html</A> <P>There are several of us now who have been very pleased with the results since we switched over to <B>ATF</B> in the clutch hydraulic system.||||reg||14
Z||000002||mutfish||11-21-1999||10:08 AM||||yeah..now that I think about it,the clutch was what I would describe as "inconsistent" even before I noticed the leak at the master cylinder. Think I'll give the atf a try...nothing ventured,nothing gained.||||reg||1
